# Orienta.me - Docker Setup

## Quick Start

```bash
# Build and start all containers
docker-compose up -d

# Run migrations
docker-compose exec app php artisan migrate

# Seed database (optional)
docker-compose exec app php artisan db:seed

# View logs
docker-compose logs -f
```

## Services

| Service | Port | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| app | 9000 | PHP-FPM |
| nginx | 80 | Web server |
| mysql | 3306 | Database |
| redis | 6379 | Cache/Queue |

## URLs

- **App:** http://localhost
- **API:** http://localhost/api

## Commands

```bash
# Restart services
docker-compose restart

# Stop services
docker-compose down

# Rebuild
docker-compose build --no-cache

# Shell into container
docker-compose exec app bash

# Run tests
docker-compose exec app php artisan test

# Queue worker
docker-compose exec app php artisan queue:work
```

## Environment

Create `.env` from example:
```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Update database config for Docker:
```env
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=db
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=orientame
DB_USERNAME=root
DB_PASSWORD=secret

REDIS_HOST=redis
CACHE_STORE=redis
QUEUE_CONNECTION=redis
SESSION_DRIVER=redis
```

## Production

For production, update `docker-compose.yml` with:
- Real domain in nginx config
- HTTPS certificates
- Secure passwords
- Backup strategy